A5  the 1-D spherical surrogate against the full 3-D solve
==============================================================================
   The parameter map is computed from k(r) = <rhat^T K rhat> and
   the exact spherical reduction.  Its error against the full
   nonlinear 3-D solve is measured here, not assumed.

   The mean matters: k varies by orders of magnitude across a shell,
   and calib.py shows the harmonic mean is the one that tracks the
   3-D answer.  Both are shown here.

